/A 1302 0 R
/Alt (The flowchart illustrates the calculation of degree of geocomplexity DG for spatial model validation. It begins with Spatial data, showing a plot representing a dependent variable and three stacked layers representing explanatory variables. A dashed arrow points right to Spatial modeling, which lists Modelling and accuracy metrics including Spatial Statistical Models, Machine Learning-Enhanced Models, Geostatistical Methods, MAE, RSME, and R squared. A dashed arrow points down from Spatial modeling to Spatial validation by degree of geocomplexity DG, which is divided into two steps. Step 1, Calculation of DG, shows Geocomplexity of dependent variable delta 0 and Geocomplexity of modeling residuals delta r. A horizontal line connects these two terms, with a downward pointing arrow from the midpoint to the equation zeta equals delta 0 minus delta r over delta 0. Step 2, Comparison between DG and non-spatial metrics, shows a Best DG model map, illustrating the different optimal model choices for different locations. To the right, a DG and accuracy metrics comparison plot is a line graph with DG on the vertical axis and R squared slash RMSE slash MAE on the horizontal axis. The line shows an increasing trend with three data points, each with vertical error bars representing 95 percent CI.)
/K 48
/P 32 0 R
/Pg 13 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
