/Alt (The three-panel map and graph shows tree biomass distribution in eastern Australia. Panel a displays a map of Australia with the eastern region highlighted as the study area, encompassing Queensland, New South Wales, and Victoria. A scale bar indicates 1000 kilometers. Panel b presents a density plot of biomass values, showing a strongly right-skewed distribution with a peak near 0 and a mean of 174.84. The horizontal axis is labeled Biomass, and the vertical axis is labeled Density. Panel c shows a detailed map of eastern Australia with numerous circular data points representing tree biomass plots. A legend indicates tree biomass in tons per hectare, ranging from 0 to 7008.2, with lighter points indicating lower biomass and darker points indicating higher biomass. A scale bar indicates 200 kilometers.)
