499 0 obj
<<
/A 1368 0 R
/Alt (The heatmap displays a correlation matrix of 19 initial environmental variables. The horizontal and vertical axes list the same variables: Temperature, Precipitation, Short wave radiation, Slope, Elevation, sin Aspect, cos Aspect, Wind speed, Soil pH, Soil depth, Soil bulk density, Soil available water capacity, Soil CEC, Soil sand, Soil silt, Soil clay, Soil carbon, Soil nitrogen, and Soil phosphorous. The matrix shows pairwise correlations with numeric values in each cell. The correlation coefficient scale below the matrix ranges from minus 1 to 1, with tick marks at minus 1, minus 0.8, minus 0.6, minus 0.4, minus 0.2, 0, 0.2, 0.4, 0.6, 0.8, and 1. The diagonal cells show a value of 1.00, representing self-correlation. Off-diagonal cells show varying correlation values, for example, Temperature and Precipitation show minus 0.29, Temperature and Short wave radiation show 0.85, and Soil carbon and Soil nitrogen show 0.84. The matrix is triangular, with values mirrored across the diagonal.)
/K 11
/P 32 0 R
/Pg 17 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
