/Alt (The 2 by 5 grid of maps shows geocomplexity of residuals for ten predictive models across a region. Each map displays data points on a landmass outline. A legend indicates geocomplexity of residuals values from 0 to 0.40, 0.40 to 0.45, 0.45 to 0.50, 0.50 to 0.55, 0.55 to 0.60, 0.60 to 0.65, 0.65 to 0.70, and 0.70 to 1.00, represented by a gradient from lighter to darker points. A scale bar indicates 0 to 500 kilometers. The models are lm, rf, xgbTree, gbm, knn, gam, pls, svmRadial, cforest, and cubist. The knn and svmRadial models show a higher concentration of darker points, indicating higher geocomplexity of residuals, particularly in the lower right region of the landmass. Other models like lm, rf, and gam show a greater prevalence of lighter points, suggesting lower geocomplexity of residuals.)
