/Alt (The four-panel figure shows optimal model performance across study area, arranged in an irregular grid. Panel a is a map of study area with sampling locations marked by symbols representing the model with the highest DG. A legend lists 10 models: cforest, gdm, pls, lm, cubist, svmRadial, gam, xgbTree, knn, and rf, each with a distinct symbol. Panels b and c are enlarged map views of two regions from panel a, showing fine-scale spatial heterogeneity in optimal model selection. Panel d is a bar graph with models on the horizontal axis and number of samples on the vertical axis, ranging from 0 to 600. The bars show the number of locations where each model achieved the highest DG: cforest 65, gbm 68, pls 96, lm 115, cubist 134, svmRadial 208, gam 265, xgbTree 389, knn 452, and rf 552. The number of samples increases from cforest to rf.)
