/Alt (The scatter plot displays DG on the vertical axis, ranging from approximately minus 1.5 to 2.5. The horizontal axis is divided into three sections: R squared from 0.1 to 0.3, RMSE from 1.30 to 1.55, and MAE from 1.00 to 1.20. Ten models are represented by different markers: cforest, cubist, gam, gbm, knn, lm, pls, rf, svmRadial, and xgbTree. Each model has a data point with vertical error bars indicating 95 percent confidence intervals. A blue line with a positive slope crosses the R squared section, a blue line with a negative slope crosses the RMSE section, and a blue line with a negative slope crosses the MAE section. For R squared, rf, cubist, and xgbTree show higher R squared values and DG values above 1. For RMSE, these models are clustered around 1.40 to 1.45 with DG values above 0. For MAE, they are around 1.05 to 1.10 with DG values above 0. Cforest shows a high R squared value around 0.3 but a DG value near 0.)
